
# Privacy Policy

**Effective Date:** 06/06/2026
**App Name:** Fastastic
**Developer:** Jamie Glazier

This Privacy Policy explains how Fastastic handles information when you use our mobile application.

## 1. Information We Collect

The App is designed to help users track fasting and lifestyle-related activity. Depending on how you use the App, you may enter information such as:

* Age or age range
* Fasting start and end times
* Tracking preferences
* Optional lifestyle tracking entries, such as caffeine, nicotine, or alcohol tracking
* App settings and progress data

We do not collect this information to diagnose, treat, prevent, or manage any medical condition.

## 2. How We Use Information

We use information entered in the App to:

* Provide tracking features
* Display fasting progress
* Save your preferences
* Restrict access when a self-reported age is below the minimum age requirement
* Improve the App experience

The App does not provide medical advice, treatment recommendations, or professional health guidance.

## 3. Self-Reported Age

The App may ask for your age or date of birth to determine whether you meet the minimum age requirement to use the App. This is based on self-reported information and is not a verified age check.

## 4. Health and Lifestyle Data

Information you enter into the App may relate to fasting, habits, or lifestyle tracking. This information is used only to provide the App’s tracking features.

You should not rely on the App as a substitute for medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional before making decisions related to fasting, nutrition, substance use, or your health.

## 5. Data Storage

Local Storage Only:
Your tracking data is stored locally on your device. We do not access, collect, or store your tracking data on our servers.

## 6. Sharing of Information

We do not sell your personal information.

We may share limited information only when necessary to:

* Operate and maintain the App
* Comply with legal obligations
* Protect the rights, safety, and security of users or the App
* Use trusted service providers that help us provide App functionality

## 7. Analytics and Crash Data

Analytics Used:
We may use analytics or crash reporting tools to understand App performance, fix bugs, and improve the user experience. These tools may collect device information, usage events, crash logs, or similar technical data.

## 8. Children’s Privacy

The App is not intended for children under 18. If a user indicates they are under the required age, access to the App may be restricted.

## 9. Your Choices

Depending on how the App stores data, you may be able to delete your data by:

* Deleting entries inside the App
* Resetting App data
* Deleting the App from your device

## 10. Data Security

We take reasonable steps to protect information handled by the App. However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## 11. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted with a new effective date. Your continued use of the App after changes are posted means you accept the updated policy.

